use std
into locks_look.amni

Imports: os, math, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes, gfx.scene3d, gfx.hair, gfx.hairdo and gfx.locks. A standalone GPU program that checks card hair (bars L5 and L6), prints one line each, then "locks look: ok", "locks look: FAILED", or "locks look: skipped" when no GPU opens. These already exist; never define them here: `gfx::open_headless(w, h) bool`, `s3d::init(w, h)`, `s3d::atmosphere(to_sun float3, a, b, c)`, `shapes::material(rgb float3, metallic f32, roughness f32) gltf::Material` (fields `shading` int, `shade_a` and `shade_c` float4, `alpha_mode` int, `base_tex` a `gltf::TexRef`), `shapes::sphere(radius f32, around int, down int, m) int`, `s3d::add(asset) int`, `s3d::place(item, matrix)`, `gfx::translate(float3)`, `s3d::view` (an `s3d::Camera { eye, target, up, fov_y (f32), near, far }`), `s3d::render(target)` taking only the target, `gfx::flush()`, `gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`, `gfx::read_pixels(texture)` giving bytes, `s3d::hdr_target()` (RGBA half floats, 8 bytes a pixel), `gltf::verts` (f32, `gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS` per vertex: normal at `gltf::AT_NRM`, tangent at `gltf::AT_TAN`, four floats), `gltf::ALPHA_OPAQUE`; `hairdo::ball(center float3, r f32)`, `hairdo::style(name)`, `hairdo::tone(name)` (fields `r`, `g`, `b` f32), `hairdo::grow(st, seed int, data)` (data a growable byte array); `locks::spec()`, `locks::build(data, s) int`, `locks::strands(size, seed) int`, `locks::material(r, g, b, tex) gltf::Material`, `locks::mesh(m) int`.

`half(lo byte, hi byte) real` decodes an IEEE half float from its two little-endian bytes: sign from the top bit, 5 exponent bits, 10 fraction bits; exponent 0 gives fraction times 2 to the minus 24; exponent 31 gives 65504; else (1024 plus fraction) times 2 to the (exponent minus 25).

`shot(eye float3, target float3, up float3, rt)` sets `s3d::view` to that camera with `fov_y` 0.42, near 0.01, far 50, then renders 2 times (render to rt then flush).

`disc(eye float3, target float3) real` is the head's projected radius in pixels for a sphere of radius 0.1 at target: with d the distance from eye to target, tan of the arcsine of 0.1 over d, times 720 over (2 times the tangent of 0.21).

`covered(a, b, rad real) real` (a and b read-only byte slices of 1280 by 720 RGBA8 pixels) is the share of pixels within 0.9 times rad of the image center (640, 360), measured from pixel centers, whose largest channel difference among red, green and blue is above 8.

`spread_ratio(px, rad real) real` (px a read-only byte slice of 1280 by 720 pixels, 8 bytes each) takes the luminance (0.2126 red plus 0.7152 green plus 0.0722 blue, each decoded with `half`) of every pixel within 0.95 times rad of the image center; p is its 95th percentile (sort a copy, take the value at index the integer part of 0.95 times the count); with weight w = luminance minus p for pixels above p, returns the weighted standard deviation of x over that of y (pixel centers; 0 when the y one is below 1e-9).

`main()`: open headless 1280 by 720 (print "locks look: skipped" and stop when it fails); `s3d::init(1280, 720)`; `s3d::temporal = 0`; `s3d::ssr_on = false`; `s3d::ssgi_on = false`; `s3d::gi_on = false`; `s3d::look.bloom = 0.0`; `s3d::atmosphere(unit3 of (0.2, 0.9, -0.4), 3.5, 1.0, 0.3)`. One render target rt of 1280 by 720 RGBA8. The head: `hairdo::ball((0, 1.6, 0), 0.1)`; a skin sphere (`shapes::sphere(0.1, 64, 32, shapes::material((0.8, 0.6, 0.5), 0, 0.6))`) added and placed at (0, 1.6, 0). sh = `hairdo::tone("auburn")`, tex = `locks::strands(512, 7)`, D grown with `hairdo::grow(hairdo::style("long waves"), 7, D)`. Hair A: `locks::build(D, locks::spec())` then `s3d::add(locks::mesh(locks::material(sh.r, sh.g, sh.b, tex)))`, placed at the origin (identity translate). Hair B (control): spec with `inner` false, `forks` 1 and `width` 0.35, built and added the same way, placed at (0, 100, 0) (out of sight).
L5 views: back eye (0, 1.6, -0.7), top eye (0, 2.3, 0.0001), both looking at (0, 1.6, 0) with up (0, 1, 0) for back and (0, 0, 1) for top. For each view: render with A placed at (0, 100, 0) (bald) and read rt's pixels; render with A at the origin, read, take `covered` with `disc`; then move A to (0, 100, 0) and B to the origin, render, read, take `covered` for the control, and move B back to (0, 100, 0) and A to the origin. Pass when both A coverages are at least 0.9 and at least one control coverage is below 0.85. Print "L5 coverage: back CB top CT control KB KT" with " ok" or " FAIL".
L6: move A to (0, 100, 0). Two spheres of radius 0.1 (128 around, 64 down): fiber with `locks::material(sh.r, sh.g, sh.b, -1)` but `alpha_mode` `gltf::ALPHA_OPAQUE` and `base_tex` texture minus 1, and standard with `shapes::material((sh.r, sh.g, sh.b), 0, 0.35)`; right after making each, set the tangent of each of its vertices (the vertex count before and after `shapes::sphere`) to the unit vector of (0, 1, 0) minus its normal times the normal's y, or (1, 0, 0) when that is shorter than 1e-4, with w 1. Add both; place the fiber one at (5, 1.6, 0) and the standard one at (5, 101.6, 0). `s3d::atmosphere(unit3 of (0.3, 0.5, 0.8), 3.5, 1.0, 0.3)`. `shot((5, 1.6, 0.6), (5, 1.6, 0), (0, 1, 0), rt)` (render to rt, never to the HDR target), then read `gfx::read_pixels(s3d::hdr_target())`, r = `spread_ratio` with `disc`. Swap the two spheres' places, the same `shot` and read again, rc. Pass when r is at least 2 and rc between 0.5 and 1.5. Print "L6 highlights: ratio R control RC" with " ok" or " FAIL".
Last print "locks look: ok" when both pass, else "locks look: FAILED".
